def card(key,name,agestr,club,pos,hook,why):
    N[0]+=1
    agestr=('age '+agestr) if agestr[:1].isdigit() else agestr
    im=('<img class="t20img" src="%s" alt="%s" loading="lazy">'%IMG[key]) if key in IMG else ''
    return ('<div class="t20c%s">'%(' ph' if im else '')+im+'<span class="t20n">%d</span><h3><a href="%s%s">%s</a></h3><div class="t20m">%s <span>&middot; %s &middot; %s</span></div><span class="t20h">%s</span><p>%s</p></div>'%(N[0],DIR,key,name,club,pos,agestr,hook,why))
b=[]
b.append('<span class="sp-kick">Long read &middot; The national team</span>')
b.append('<p class="sp-stand">On Monday we told the stories of four players Thailand lost, or nearly lost. This is the list of the ones it should not. Twenty footballers with Thai heritage, from Malmö to Orange County, who could be wearing the shirt by the 2030 World Cup qualifiers. But a diaspora plan only works if it is built around a Thai core, and if the FA is prepared to pay for something as ordinary as Thai lessons.</p>')
b.append(H("Where we left off"))
b.append(P("""<a href="https://footballsiam.com/the-ones-that-got-away-thailand-diaspora/">The ones that got away</a> set Felix Paschke, never asked and now retired at 23, beside Erawan Garnier, who was caught early, Stipe Ukich, whom New Zealand reached first, and Eric Kahl, who is still saying not yet. The lesson was that the federation waits, and that waiting costs players. We promised a list of who to call next. It ran long."""))
b.append(P("""To build it we started with every post on <a href="https://www.instagram.com/half_thailand.123/">@half_thailand.123</a>, the account that has spent years tracking luk khrueng footballers around the world, and then went well beyond it: Transfermarkt, club and federation websites, FotMob, and the Thai and local press, checking every player and adding ones the account had not covered. The result is our new <a href="https://footballsiam.com/dual-heritage-players/">Dual Heritage map</a>: 142 men aged 15 and over with a Thai parent, 11 of them already senior internationals. These are the twenty we would be on the phone to now."""))
b.append(H("How we chose"))
b.append(P("""Each player has a Thai parent, or in two cases Thai heritage through a grandparent, which we have marked. Each is playing first-team football or is in a serious academy, and none is tied to another country by a competitive senior cap. Youth caps for Sweden, Switzerland or Belgium do not bind anyone; under FIFA's rules a player can switch once if he has not played more than three competitive senior matches for his first country, all before turning 21. We have left out players already capped by Thailand at senior level, and Kahl and Ukich, whom we covered on Monday. The order is urgency, not talent: who is closest to being lost."""))
b.append('<div class="t20band">Call now: ready for senior football</div><div class="t20">')
b.append(card('skogmar','Adrian Skogmar','%d'%age('2005-11-23'),'Malmö FF','Midfielder','Sweden U21','Two Allsvenskan titles and Champions League football before he turned 21. Reported to have met Anthony Hudson last December; his family say his focus is Sweden. The most talented player on this list, and the hardest sell.'))
b.append(card('warneryd','Alexander Warneryd','%d'%age('2005-08-21'),'Tromsø','Full-back','Sweden U21','His mother is from Prachinburi. Reported in March to have agreed to play for Thailand, but he was not in September\'s squad. If the deal is real, it needs a date on it.'))
b.append(card('skaarud','Daniel Skaarud','%d'%age('2007-09-17'),'Sandefjord','Winger','Norway U15 to U18','An Eliteserien debut for Lillestrøm at 15, a reported €1.2m move to Ajax, and now back in Norway\'s top flight on a deal to 2030. Thai mother, never approached as far as we can find.'))
b.append(card('constable','Scott Constable','%d'%age('2007-08-22'),'Arbroath, on loan from Dundee United','Right-back or holding midfielder','Scotland U19','Holds Thai citizenship and has said he would be happy to play for Thailand\'s under-23s. Scotland have capped him at youth level; that is not a reason to wait.'))
b.append(card('gurd','Aaron Gurd','%d'%age('2001-09-18'),'Sydney Olympic, on loan from Sydney FC','Centre-back','No other caps','Spent last season at Kanchanaburi Power, where his Thai passport made him a local player. A senior centre-back with no other international ties, already proven in Thai League 1.'))
b.append(card('agelin','Theodor Agelin','%d'%age('2003-08-29'),'Jerv, on loan from Sandefjord','Full-back','No other caps','Thai mother from Chiang Mai, Norwegian and Swedish passports, and no international football for anyone. Left-sided full-backs are not a position Thailand can afford to ignore.'))
b.append(card('kallman','Liam Källman','%d'%age('2006-02-23'),'Vasalunds IF','Right-back','Sweden U16 to U18','A Hammarby academy product who now plays senior football in Sweden\'s third tier. He holds Thai citizenship already; the paperwork that held up others is not a problem here.'))
b.append(card('lhakpa','Norbu Lhakpa','%d'%age('2008-06-27'),'FC Zürich U21','Winger','Switzerland U19','Thai and Tibetan heritage, a Thai passport, and a goal in a Swiss Cup final at under-19 level. Switzerland are using him now. Thailand should be asking now.'))
b.append(card('micah-duchowny','Micah Duchowny','23','Los Cabos United','Right-back','Thailand youth','Playing regularly at right-back for a competitive Los Cabos United side in Mexico, and the older brother of Jonah, who featured on Monday. He has already played for Thailand at youth level. At 23, the senior call should come now.'))
b.append('</div><div class="t20band">Next window: the contested teenagers</div><div class="t20">')
b.append(card('marinc','Apolo Marinch','born 2010','Orange County','Winger','USA U15 camp','Signed a professional contract in the USL Championship in September 2025 and has played for the first team this year. The United States have already had him in camp. Of everyone here, he is the one most likely to be gone within two years.'))
b.append(card('waimer','Joey Waimer','born 2009','Augsburg U19','Centre-back','UAE U17','Thai mother, German and Emirati passports, and a UAE under-17 cap that came against Thailand. Three countries want him; only one has not asked.'))
b.append(card('terrell','Lyndon Turrell','born 2009','Leicester City U18','Attacking midfielder','Gibraltar U19','Has trained with Thailand\'s under-17s and scored against India, but has played for Gibraltar at every youth level. A Leicester academy player who has shown he wants Thailand deserves a clear plan.'))
b.append(card('brisco','Yanis Brisco','born 2010','Charleroi U18','Winger','Belgium U15','A Belgian youth international with a Thai mother, back at Charleroi after two years at Club Brugge. Belgium\'s pathway is crowded; Thailand\'s is not.'))
b.append(card('theeten','Tanthai Theeten','born 2009','Gent U18','Left-back','Belgium U16','Another Belgian youth international, in Gent\'s academy since 2023. His first name is Thai; the next call should be too.'))
b.append(card('spuhler','Sven Spühler','%d'%age('2008-01-28'),'FC Zürich U19','Right-back','Switzerland U16','A Thai mother and a place in one of Switzerland\'s best academies. One Swiss youth cap so far, which means the door is wide open.'))
b.append('</div><div class="t20band">Keep close: in the system, or nearly</div><div class="t20">')
b.append(card('mexes','Silva Mexes','born 2010','Leeds United U18','Winger','Thailand U17','Scored for Thailand at the 2025 AFC U17 Asian Cup and has just moved from Manchester United to Leeds. The son of the former Wales striker Robert Earnshaw, he is also eligible for Wales and Zambia. Thailand has him; it needs to keep him.'))
b.append(card('fletcher','Jake Fletcher','born 2008','Leicester City U18','Centre-forward','Thailand U17','At Leicester since he was 11, three goals in his first four games this season and a Premier League 2 debut. Called up by Thailand at under-17 level; the under-20s should be next.'))
b.append(card('reinat','Orin Reinat','%d'%age('2008-07-31'),'OH Leuven U23','Defensive midfielder','No other caps','Through the Westerlo, Genk and Anderlecht academies to a Leuven contract until 2029. Belgian, Puerto Rican and Thai heritage. Nobody has capped him yet.'))
b.append(card('noser','Jeremy Noser','born 2009','FC Linth 04, on loan from Winterthur','Winger','No other caps','Already playing senior football as a teenager, on loan in the Swiss fifth tier. Holds a Thai passport under the name Phumin.'))
b.append(card('kinnavong','Jordan Kinnavong','%d'%age('2008-01-10'),'SF Baumberg U19','Winger','Albania U17 friendlies','Thai and Lao heritage through his mother, two friendly caps for Albania, and on record saying he hopes to play for Thailand. The easiest yes on this list.'))
b.append('</div>')
b.append(H("A Thai core, not a Thai shell"))
b.append(P("""None of this is an argument for doing what Indonesia did. When Patrick Kluivert named a provisional squad in March 2025, 19 of the 30 players were naturalised (<a href="https://databoks.katadata.co.id/en/consumer-services/statistics/67cfb0427ae59/indonesia-national-team-provisional-squad-march-2025-63-naturalized">Databoks</a>). It worked on the pitch; it beat Thailand in the FIFA ASEAN Cup final this month. But it is a national team assembled rather than grown, and Thailand has a league, an academy system and a football culture that deserve better than to be bypassed."""))
b.append(P("""Our view is that Thailand should keep a core of players developed in Thailand by Thai clubs, the majority of any squad, and use the diaspora to add what the domestic game is not yet producing: a left-back here, a centre-back with Champions League minutes there. The Thai League gets a reason to keep investing in youth, the luk khrueng players arrive into a team with an identity rather than replacing it, and supporters still recognise the side as theirs. Every player above has a Thai parent. That is the line Thailand has drawn, and it is the right one."""))
b.append(H("Pay for the lessons"))
b.append(P("""Integration is where the plan succeeds or fails, and it starts with language. Many of the players on this list grew up speaking Swedish, German, English or French at home. A dressing room, a team talk, a press conference and a terrace all happen in Thai. A player who cannot follow them is a guest, however good he is."""))
b.append(P("""So here is a cheap, practical proposal: the FA should pay for Thai lessons for every mixed-heritage player it calls up who does not already speak the language, from his first youth camp. Online tutoring for the player and, for the younger ones, a parent; a short cultural induction at each camp; a buddy from the Thai-raised players in the squad. The cost is a rounding error next to a single scouting trip to Scandinavia. The return is a player who feels Thai in the room, not just on the passport."""))
b.append(P("""The players themselves suggest the will is there. Jude Soonsup-Bell, capped by England at four youth levels, was asked whether he had needed persuading to choose Thailand."""))
b.append(Q('"I didn\'t need convincing. I wanted to play for Thailand."','Jude Soonsup-Bell, to <a href="https://www.livescore.com/en/news/football/club-world-cup/former-chelsea-academy-graduate-jude-soonsup-bell-sets-sights-on-silverware-as-thailand-target-fifa-asean-cup-glory-goal/">LiveScore</a>'))
b.append(P("""Wanting to play for a country and belonging in its dressing room are not the same thing, and the gap between them is exactly the kind of thing a federation can close with a little money and a little thought."""))
b.append(H("Have we missed anyone?"))
b.append(P("""This list, and the <a href="https://footballsiam.com/dual-heritage-players/">Dual Heritage map</a> behind it, rests on far more than one Instagram account. We began with @half_thailand.123 and then worked through Transfermarkt, club and federation websites, FotMob and the Thai and local press, checking every name we could. Even so, a list like this is never finished, and players move every window."""))
b.append(P("""Are you on this list, or should you be? If you are a player with a Thai parent, or you know one, message us on LINE or through our social channels and we will add you. Monday's piece ended with a short list. This one is longer, and the clock is running on all of it."""))
b.append('<p class="sp-end">Player details are from Transfermarkt, club and federation sites, FotMob, Thai and local press and the Instagram account @half_thailand.123, checked in October 2026; each name links to its profile on our Dual Heritage map, with sources. Ages are as of 13 October 2026. The views on squad composition and language lessons are Football Siam\'s.</p>')
